package CanvasNet {
    part def HelpTopics {
        doc /* The tree of help cards of the tool, shipped inside the tool as embedded Markdown files so that it works offline and matches the installed version. A card is one short Markdown file with YAML front matter (title, summary, aliases, children, see-also, and examples); its identifier is its path, so the folders of the files are the tree. The fifteen root cards are the help topics in a fixed order (scad, vega-lite, mermaid, svg, pdf, pptx, vsdx, raster, style, composition, positions, json, errors, limits, and files), with aliases (for example openscad, vl, mmd, powerpoint, visio, and png or jpg for raster); a large topic is split into cards below it, such as mermaid gantt and mermaid gantt settings, so every card stays under 6,000 characters and an index card under 3,500. The front matter is read by a strict parser of a small YAML subset, without a package dependency, that reports anything else with the file and the line; the loader checks that the roots are the topics, that the children of a card are exactly the files of its folder, that every See also entry names another card, and that names, aliases, and example names are unique where they must be. The tree of an input format has the sections Supported, Unsupported, Options, Diagnostics (and how --strict treats them), and Known differences, and at least two examples; each drawing format (scad, vega-lite, mermaid, and svg) also has a style card and a composition card, linked both ways with the style and composition topics, which give verified advice on palette, fonts, size, backgrounds, and checking the picture, and on combining diagrams, charts, models, and pages in one figure. The numbers in the text are tokens resolved from the constants of the code when a card loads. An example is source text (shipped as a file and verified to render with --strict without a diagnostic, including a styled Mermaid flowchart and a styled Vega-Lite chart), a snippet (text that refers to other files, such as the embed, embed-pages, pictures, and report figures, verified by a test that renders it with its sibling files), or a command line. The unit resolves a card by a path of names or aliases ignoring case (an unknown card below a card is a usage error that lists the cards at that level), and renders a card as plain text (its title, summary, and body as written, then the cards below it, its examples, and its See also links as exact commands with the summaries of their targets; deterministic, without color codes) or as a JSON document (kind card), the whole tree (kind topics), and the examples (kinds examples and example). The content is verified against the code (the options of the render command, every error code, the cited diagnostic identifiers and what triggers them, the limits, and every command line), against the user guides (the Mermaid tables, the flatten reference, and the file access reference, row for row), and, for the style advice, against the renderer. It is used by the CommandRegistry unit, which owns the help command, and by the help examples self-test of the Validation unit. The positions topic has cards for the selectors (the grammar, the matching, the limits, and quoting for bash, PowerShell 7.3 or later, and cmd), the Mermaid and Vega-Lite kinds, ids, and attachment points, and the geometry, with its limits resolved from the tokens positionsMax, positionsMaxSelectors, positionsMaxSelectorLength, positionsMaxPredicates, and positionsMaxDataFields; it is linked with the framed-figure, anchors, and composition cards, and the framed-figure card teaches to read positions[].pixel of the picture rendered at the size of its image, with the grid and inspect pixel as the fallback, and an example (framed-flow) whose arrows end on those positions. The svg bindings card documents the SVG position bindings, and the framed-figure card recommends a binding first. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/HelpTopics.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/HelpTopics.FrontMatter.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/HelpTopics.Render.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool/Commands/Help/ (the embedded card files and the examples in Help/Examples/) */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.FrontMatter.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Tree.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Guidance.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Triggers.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Positions.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpCardText.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/InputFragmentTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Tool.Tests/Commands/HelpTopicsTests.Bindings.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-tool/commands/help-topics.yaml */
    }
}
